# Risk register — the lender IM's qualitative project-risk matrix (#C8). CCCDIR: the risks
# are config-authored (per-project analyst content), not hardcoded in Python; the report
# layer only renders them. `severity` is the RESIDUAL rating after mitigation
# (low | medium | high) and drives the badge colour. Seeded with the real DutchBay risk
# profile of a flat-nominal-LKR tariff financed with hard-currency debt.
risk_register:
  - category: "Revenue / FX"
    risk: >
      The PPA tariff is fixed in nominal LKR with no escalation or FX indexation, while
      debt and sponsor returns are measured in USD — LKR depreciation erodes the hard-
      currency value of every future rupee of revenue.
    mitigation: >
      FX path stressed to CBSL/IMF projections; debt sized off the LKR-denominated DSCR;
      the resulting negative equity IRR is disclosed to sponsors rather than masked.
    severity: "high"
